\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \emph  {Top (collapse branch):} Collapse of the pure-quadrupole arm ($\varepsilon _2=0.01$, no radial kick). (a)~Minimal-surface areal radius (ink) and the scan's MOTS (gold) from $t=33$: $R$ $3.80\to 2.41$, $M_{\rm  MS}$ $1.90\to 1.24$. Grey: the unkicked level-4 twin, which inflates on its own seed; this arm leaves it by $10\%$ only at $t=42$---the second-order drive of the pure quadrupole. (b)--(d)~Global $\min \alpha $, $\min \chi $ (the origin, the far side's compactified infinity) and $\max |K|$; the violent phase spans $t=45$--$55$. (e),(f)~Radial profiles over 128{} shells, $t=33$--$55$ (light = early): $|K|$ grows inward while $\alpha $ pinches to zero at the centre. Constraint norms: Fig.~\ref {fig:constraints}(c). The collapse ends in a black hole that consumes its supporting field. \emph  {Bottom (inflation branch):} The inflating throat ($\varepsilon =-10^{-2}$; $L=512$ octant, finest $\Delta x=1/16$) to $t=218$. (a)~Neck areal radius in the full metric, $3.81\to 14.5$; gold, the exponential onset, $\tau =5.7$ over $t=16$--$28$; shaded, exponential growth in the neck's proper time ($t=16$--$40$, gold) and the slower growth in $t$ once $1{+}\log $ freezes the neck's clock (grey). (b)~Over that window the neck's proper-time rate is $HR_0=1.22$ (local $1.0$--$1.3$), against the massless throat's $Ha=1.1$~\cite  {shinkai2002} and the linear mode's $1.30$. (c)~The $\theta _l=0$ horizon stays on the neck; $\theta _k=0$ runs out to $R\approx 73$ by $t=212$. (d)~The lapse at the neck falls $0.57\to 0.015$; dashed, its minimum on the finest box. (e),(f)~$\max |K|$ and $\min \chi $ on the finest box, around the origin. (g),(h)~$\chi $ and $\alpha $ per shell (light = early): the $\chi $ peak moves out with the neck. Constraint norms: Fig.~\ref {fig:constraints}(d). The throat keeps growing, anti-trapped; its onset is at the linear rate.}}{9}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:single_collapse}{{3}{9}{\emph {Top (collapse branch):} Collapse of the pure-quadrupole arm ($\varepsilon _2=\clmPureQuadAmpCaption $, no radial kick). (a)~Minimal-surface areal radius (ink) and the scan's MOTS (gold) from $t=\clmPureQuadMotsTime $: $R$ $\clmPureQuadMotsRStart \to \clmPureQuadMotsREnd $, $M_{\rm MS}$ $\clmPureQuadMotsMStart \to \clmPureQuadMotsMEnd $. Grey: the unkicked level-4 twin, which inflates on its own seed; this arm leaves it by $10\%$ only at $t=\clmPureQuadDeparture $---the second-order drive of the pure quadrupole. (b)--(d)~Global $\min \alpha $, $\min \chi $ (the origin, the far side's compactified infinity) and $\max |K|$; the violent phase spans $t=\clmCollapseViolentLo $--$\clmCollapseViolentHi $. (e),(f)~Radial profiles over \clmCollapseShells {} shells, $t=33$--$55$ (light = early): $|K|$ grows inward while $\alpha $ pinches to zero at the centre. Constraint norms: Fig.~\ref {fig:constraints}(c). The collapse ends in a black hole that consumes its supporting field. \emph {Bottom (inflation branch):} The inflating throat ($\varepsilon =-10^{-2}$; $L=\clmFourBoxL $ octant, finest $\Delta x=\clmFourFinestDx $) to $t=\clmFourWall $. (a)~Neck areal radius in the full metric, $\clmFourRStart \to \clmFourRWall $; gold, the exponential onset, $\tau =\clmFourOnsetEfold $ over $t=\clmFourOnsetLo $--$\clmFourOnsetHi $; shaded, exponential growth in the neck's proper time ($t=\clmFourSHWinLo $--$\clmFourSHWinHi $, gold) and the slower growth in $t$ once $1{+}\log $ freezes the neck's clock (grey). (b)~Over that window the neck's proper-time rate is $HR_0=\clmFourSHRate $ (local $\clmFourSHLocalLo $--$\clmFourSHLocalHi $), against the massless throat's $Ha=\clmSHMassless $~\cite {shinkai2002} and the linear mode's $\clmFourLinearRate $. (c)~The $\theta _l=0$ horizon stays on the neck; $\theta _k=0$ runs out to $R\approx \clmFourHorizonR $ by $t=\clmFourHorizonTime $. (d)~The lapse at the neck falls $\clmFourLapseStart \to \clmFourLapseEnd $; dashed, its minimum on the finest box. (e),(f)~$\max |K|$ and $\min \chi $ on the finest box, around the origin. (g),(h)~$\chi $ and $\alpha $ per shell (light = early): the $\chi $ peak moves out with the neck. Constraint norms: Fig.~\ref {fig:constraints}(d). The throat keeps growing, anti-trapped; its onset is at the linear rate}{figure.3}{}}
\newlabel{fig:single_inflation}{{3}{9}{\emph {Top (collapse branch):} Collapse of the pure-quadrupole arm ($\varepsilon _2=\clmPureQuadAmpCaption $, no radial kick). (a)~Minimal-surface areal radius (ink) and the scan's MOTS (gold) from $t=\clmPureQuadMotsTime $: $R$ $\clmPureQuadMotsRStart \to \clmPureQuadMotsREnd $, $M_{\rm MS}$ $\clmPureQuadMotsMStart \to \clmPureQuadMotsMEnd $. Grey: the unkicked level-4 twin, which inflates on its own seed; this arm leaves it by $10\%$ only at $t=\clmPureQuadDeparture $---the second-order drive of the pure quadrupole. (b)--(d)~Global $\min \alpha $, $\min \chi $ (the origin, the far side's compactified infinity) and $\max |K|$; the violent phase spans $t=\clmCollapseViolentLo $--$\clmCollapseViolentHi $. (e),(f)~Radial profiles over \clmCollapseShells {} shells, $t=33$--$55$ (light = early): $|K|$ grows inward while $\alpha $ pinches to zero at the centre. Constraint norms: Fig.~\ref {fig:constraints}(c). The collapse ends in a black hole that consumes its supporting field. \emph {Bottom (inflation branch):} The inflating throat ($\varepsilon =-10^{-2}$; $L=\clmFourBoxL $ octant, finest $\Delta x=\clmFourFinestDx $) to $t=\clmFourWall $. (a)~Neck areal radius in the full metric, $\clmFourRStart \to \clmFourRWall $; gold, the exponential onset, $\tau =\clmFourOnsetEfold $ over $t=\clmFourOnsetLo $--$\clmFourOnsetHi $; shaded, exponential growth in the neck's proper time ($t=\clmFourSHWinLo $--$\clmFourSHWinHi $, gold) and the slower growth in $t$ once $1{+}\log $ freezes the neck's clock (grey). (b)~Over that window the neck's proper-time rate is $HR_0=\clmFourSHRate $ (local $\clmFourSHLocalLo $--$\clmFourSHLocalHi $), against the massless throat's $Ha=\clmSHMassless $~\cite {shinkai2002} and the linear mode's $\clmFourLinearRate $. (c)~The $\theta _l=0$ horizon stays on the neck; $\theta _k=0$ runs out to $R\approx \clmFourHorizonR $ by $t=\clmFourHorizonTime $. (d)~The lapse at the neck falls $\clmFourLapseStart \to \clmFourLapseEnd $; dashed, its minimum on the finest box. (e),(f)~$\max |K|$ and $\min \chi $ on the finest box, around the origin. (g),(h)~$\chi $ and $\alpha $ per shell (light = early): the $\chi $ peak moves out with the neck. Constraint norms: Fig.~\ref {fig:constraints}(d). The throat keeps growing, anti-trapped; its onset is at the linear rate}{figure.3}{}}
