\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The head-on merger ($d=8$ from rest, $p=0$, opposite signs) on matched, solved data ($M_{\rm  ADM}=2.3573$), and the black hole it makes. One evolution, drawn across its three legs (faint dashed rules at the seams, $t=35$ and $50.8$; levels named in each panel): the level-5 leg reaches contact and then dies of a NaN in the metric component $h_{11}$ at the merged core at $t=38.845$---inside the MOTS, the censored interior failure of Sec.~\ref {sec:spiral:wall}, its overrun drawn grey to the death cross in (c)--(e); the level-6 leg restarts from leg 1's $t=35$ checkpoint and walks through the wall; the level-4 leg carries the remnant to $t=100$ with no NaN, the fine levels no longer needed once the wall is crossed. In-code $\Psi _4$ is identical on both overlaps: the seams carry nothing. (a)~Areal radius and (b)~Misner--Sharp mass of the common MOTS. Gold: the spectral finder's history (Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:mots}, one row per plotfile, the three replay legs joined), born at $t=18$ with $R=5.634$ ($M_{\rm  MS}=2.817$) and settling---monotone to $0.08\%$ per row---onto the Schwarzschild sphere of the pair's mass: $R=4.7787$ and $M_{\rm  MS}=2.3894$ at $t=100$, $1.4\%$ above $2M_{\rm  ADM}$ and $1.4\%$ above $M_{\rm  ADM}$. Grey dashes: the round star scan, the demoted inner bound (Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:mots})---it finds the birth $4$ units late and $11\%$ small, goes blind over $t=26$--$35$ while the surface is deformed, and wobbles about the settle; its rows are joined only within a contiguous run, never across the gap. Rules: one isolated throat, $R_\star =3.8895$; $\sqrt  2R_\star $, a sphere with both throats' area; $2M_{\rm  ADM}$ ($M_{\rm  ADM}$ in (b)). (c)~Separation of the $\chi $ pits. (d)~$\max |K|$. (e)~Grid maxima of $|\phi |$ (solid) and $|\Pi |$ (dashed): the field is swallowed. Gold dotted rule: horizon birth.}}{13}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:headon_collapse}{{5}{13}{The head-on merger ($d=\clmHeadonSeparation $ from rest, $p=0$, opposite signs) on matched, solved data ($M_{\rm ADM}=\clmHeadonCsmAdmMass $), and the black hole it makes. One evolution, drawn across its three legs (faint dashed rules at the seams, $t=\clmHeadonCsmSeamOne $ and $\clmHeadonCsmSeamTwo $; levels named in each panel): the level-5 leg reaches contact and then dies of a NaN in the metric component $h_{11}$ at the merged core at $t=\clmHeadonCsmNanTime $---inside the MOTS, the censored interior failure of Sec.~\ref {sec:spiral:wall}, its overrun drawn grey to the death cross in (c)--(e); the level-6 leg restarts from leg 1's $t=35$ checkpoint and walks through the wall; the level-4 leg carries the remnant to $t=100$ with no NaN, the fine levels no longer needed once the wall is crossed. In-code $\Psi _4$ is identical on both overlaps: the seams carry nothing. (a)~Areal radius and (b)~Misner--Sharp mass of the common MOTS. Gold: the spectral finder's history (Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:mots}, one row per plotfile, the three replay legs joined), born at $t=\clmHeadonCsmMotsTime $ with $R=\clmHeadonCsmMotsRadius $ ($M_{\rm MS}=\clmHeadonCsmMotsMass $) and settling---monotone to $\clmHeadonCsmRowWobble \%$ per row---onto the Schwarzschild sphere of the pair's mass: $R=\clmHeadonCsmEndRadius $ and $M_{\rm MS}=\clmHeadonCsmEndMass $ at $t=100$, $\clmHeadonCsmEndOverSchw \%$ above $2M_{\rm ADM}$ and $\clmHeadonCsmEndMassOverAdm \%$ above $M_{\rm ADM}$. Grey dashes: the round star scan, the demoted inner bound (Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:mots})---it finds the birth $\clmHeadonScanLate $ units late and $\clmHeadonScanSmall \%$ small, goes blind over $t=26$--$35$ while the surface is deformed, and wobbles about the settle; its rows are joined only within a contiguous run, never across the gap. Rules: one isolated throat, $R_\star =\clmRstar $; $\sqrt 2R_\star $, a sphere with both throats' area; $2M_{\rm ADM}$ ($M_{\rm ADM}$ in (b)). (c)~Separation of the $\chi $ pits. (d)~$\max |K|$. (e)~Grid maxima of $|\phi |$ (solid) and $|\Pi |$ (dashed): the field is swallowed. Gold dotted rule: horizon birth}{figure.5}{}}
