\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The orbital merger ($d=6$, tangential $p=0.10$, opposite signs, boosted mode-3 data) carried through its merger wall, and the black hole it settles to. One evolution composed across its legs (faint dashed rules at the restarts, $t=25$, $30$ and $35$; levels named in the panels): level 5 from $t=0$, stopped at $t=26.26$ as the merged core's $K$ ran away; the $\sigma _{\rm  KO}=1.0$ leg; the $\chi $-floor crossing leg; the level-4 settle leg to $t=100$, no NaN. (a)~Areal radius and (b)~Misner--Sharp mass of the common MOTS: gold, the spectral finder's history (Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:mots}), born at $t=13$ and settling from above onto the head-on remnant's values (dash-dotted rules, $R=4.7787$; $M_{\rm  MS}=2.3894$ in (b)). Dotted rules in (a): one isolated throat, $R_\star $; $\sqrt  2R_\star $, both throats' area. (c)~Separation of the $\chi $ pits (grey: leg 1's overrun past its restart checkpoint). (d)~The wall: $\max |K|$ of every arm---the used legs in ink; the level-6 and level-7 diagnostic restarts (grey dashed) die at $t=29.4$ and, \emph  {earlier}, $27.5$, each a single-cell $h_{11}$ NaN at the core's centre with the global norms clean to the last step; the $\sigma $ arm (grey solid) clears the $K$ wall and dies at the same cell at $t=30.5$ (death crosses); the $\chi $-floor and settle legs carry the history through. (e)~Grid maxima of $|\phi |$ (solid) and $|\Pi |$ (dashed): the field is swallowed. Gold dotted rule: horizon birth.}}{15}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:spiral_collapse}{{6}{15}{The orbital merger ($d=6$, tangential $p=\clmDSixP $, opposite signs, boosted mode-3 data) carried through its merger wall, and the black hole it settles to. One evolution composed across its legs (faint dashed rules at the restarts, $t=\clmMergerSeamOne $, $\clmMergerSeamTwo $ and $\clmMergerSeamThree $; levels named in the panels): level 5 from $t=0$, stopped at $t=\clmMergerLegOneStop $ as the merged core's $K$ ran away; the $\sigma _{\rm KO}=1.0$ leg; the $\chi $-floor crossing leg; the level-4 settle leg to $t=100$, no NaN. (a)~Areal radius and (b)~Misner--Sharp mass of the common MOTS: gold, the spectral finder's history (Sec.~\ref {sec:setup:mots}), born at $t=\clmMergerMotsTime $ and settling from above onto the head-on remnant's values (dash-dotted rules, $R=\clmHeadonCsmEndRadius $; $M_{\rm MS}=\clmHeadonCsmEndMass $ in (b)). Dotted rules in (a): one isolated throat, $R_\star $; $\sqrt 2R_\star $, both throats' area. (c)~Separation of the $\chi $ pits (grey: leg 1's overrun past its restart checkpoint). (d)~The wall: $\max |K|$ of every arm---the used legs in ink; the level-6 and level-7 diagnostic restarts (grey dashed) die at $t=\clmMergerLvlSixDeath $ and, \emph {earlier}, $\clmMergerLvlSevenDeath $, each a single-cell $h_{11}$ NaN at the core's centre with the global norms clean to the last step; the $\sigma $ arm (grey solid) clears the $K$ wall and dies at the same cell at $t=\clmMergerSigDeath $ (death crosses); the $\chi $-floor and settle legs carry the history through. (e)~Grid maxima of $|\phi |$ (solid) and $|\Pi |$ (dashed): the field is swallowed. Gold dotted rule: horizon birth}{figure.6}{}}
